cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "piiscope: find, score and remediate personal data in files and databases"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Sozudogru
    given-names: Baris
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0002-6506-1720"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22071806"
repository-code: "https://github.com/barissozudogru/piiscope"
url: "https://github.com/barissozudogru/piiscope"
abstract: >-
  piiscope finds personal data in datasets and measures privacy risks across
  global jurisdictions. It scans tabular data or free text to locate direct
  identifiers and calculates k-anonymity, l-diversity and t-closeness on
  quasi-identifiers. Findings can be remediated by applying hashing,
  generalisation or tokenisation directly to the target columns.
keywords:
  - personal data
  - privacy risk
  - k-anonymity
  - l-diversity
  - t-closeness
  - de-identification
  - GDPR
  - data protection
license: Apache-2.0
version: 1.3.0
date-released: "2026-08-26"
